{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7ac2c7ec9e5841f462fd548b2adbe08c1ec463d3900447ddd03e9345d1fe8c94","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot-janitor / disk-pressure management","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","DEFAULT_FREE_WATERMARK_BYTES","DEFAULT_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT","free_watermark_pct","REBAR_GATE_FREE_WATERMARK_PCT","src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","run_gc","_gc_pass","infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf","rebar-root-disk-pressure","JanitorConfig","shutil.disk_usage"],"problem_keywords":["disk pressure","root volume","garbage collection","space reclaim","watermark","snapshot storage","janitor","threshold trigger"],"propositions":["The snapshot janitor's absolute 2-GiB free-space watermark is disk-size-blind and unreachable on small volumes (93.3% used on a 30-GiB root), sitting above the 85% alarm threshold and preventing reclaim before exhaustion.","Adding a volume-relative percentage-based watermark term allows the trigger to scale with volume size and engage below the alarm floor without breaking existing deployments.","The janitor must use hysteresis with a 5-point target margin above the trigger to avoid re-firing every 300 seconds and to reclaim past the threshold rather than stopping at it.","The new free_watermark_pct knob must be a whole integer (matching the existing int-only config seam) and bounded to 0–50% to prevent footguns like triggering on the entire volume."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787332538415443001,"uuid":"e8b6a983-45d0-447d-9d07-53b1c0060eb2"}